From: k4 <k4@local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ksu: hook the native arm64 newfstatat and statx syscalls

The ReSukiSU manual hooks ("kernel: add ReSukiSU manual hooks", 2649a3036)
put ksu_handle_stat() into sys_fstatat64 (32-bit) and
compat_sys_newfstatat (not even wired into the arm64 compat table), but
not into the native SYSCALL_DEFINE4(newfstatat) that every 64-bit bionic
stat()/lstat()/fstatat() uses on arm64 (SYSCALLS.TXT:
"fstatat64|fstatat:newfstatat(...) lp64").

mksh's search_access() does stat(fn) first and only then access(fn) /
execve(fn); with the stat unhooked, stat("/system/bin/su") returns ENOENT
and the shell prints "su: inaccessible or not found" (exit 127) before
the hooked faccessat/execve paths are ever reached, so sucompat never
fires for 64-bit callers (adb shell, terminal apps, root checkers) and no
KernelSU log line is printed.

Hook the native newfstatat like upstream's manual-integration guide does,
and statx as well (toybox stat, Rust std::fs::metadata and other statx
users) so they see /system/bin/su too.
---
diff --git a/fs/stat.c b/fs/stat.c
index 3c948c044..8e73211af 100755
--- a/fs/stat.c
+++ b/fs/stat.c
@@ -375,6 +375,10 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE4(newfstatat, int, dfd, const char __user *, filename,
 	struct kstat stat;
 	int error;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK // 64-bit su: bionic stat()/lstat()/fstatat() on arm64
+	ksu_handle_stat(&dfd, &filename, &flag);
+#endif
+
 	error = vfs_fstatat(dfd, filename, &stat, flag);
 	if (error)
 		return error;
@@ -603,6 +607,10 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE5(statx,
 	if ((flags & AT_STATX_SYNC_TYPE) == AT_STATX_SYNC_TYPE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK // statx() users (toybox stat, Rust std::fs::metadata, ...)
+	ksu_handle_stat(&dfd, &filename, (int *)&flags);
+#endif
+
 	error = vfs_statx(dfd, filename, flags, &stat, mask);
 	if (error)
 		return error;
